--- body ---
## Context

Escaped scope from ticket 0071 triage. Three string-only fixes with no logic
changes, grouped as P1 because they are actively wrong or were missed by PR #78.

Items from 0071:
- A: per-command usage strings still use `<arg>` angle brackets after PR #78
  fixed printUsage(). Files: close.go, validate.go, new.go, log.go.
- F: `erg new` prints only the filename on success; every other mutating command
  prints a status verb first (CLOSED, LOGGED, ARCHIVED). Should print `CREATED`.
- G: `SKIPPED %s (blocking %s)` is ambiguous — "blocking" does not say which
  ticket is waiting on which. The ticket being archived is needed by another open
  ticket. Should read `SKIPPED %s (needed by %s)`.

## Actions

1. In `close.go`: `"Usage: erg close <id|file> <reason> [dir]"` → `"Usage: erg close ID|FILE REASON [DIR]"`
2. In `validate.go`: `"Usage: erg validate <file ...>"` → `"Usage: erg validate FILE..."`
3. In `new.go`: `"Usage: erg new <title> [dir]"` → `"Usage: erg new TITLE [DIR]"`
4. In `log.go`: `"Usage: erg log <id> <line> [dir]"` → `"Usage: erg log ID LINE [DIR]"`
5. In `new.go`: change filename-only print to `fmt.Printf("CREATED %s\n", path)`
6. In `archive.go`: `"SKIPPED %s (blocking %s)"` → `"SKIPPED %s (needed by %s)"`

## Test

Extend `tests/test_help.sh`: assert no `<` or `>` in per-command error output
(run each command with wrong args, check stderr).

Add to `tests/test_new.sh`: `erg new "foo"` output matches `^CREATED `.

Add to `tests/test_archive.sh`: assert "needed by" appears when a blocker
prevents archiving.

## Exit criteria

- `make test` passes.
- `grep -r '<\|>' tickets/tools/go/*.go` returns no matches inside usage strings.
- `erg new TITLE` output starts with `CREATED`.
- `erg archive` blocked output contains "needed by", not "blocking".
